map.：某规划区常住人口 50000 人，总用地 500 ha，其中居住用地 250:
A planning area has a permanent population of 50,000 with 500 ha of total land, of which 250 ha is residential:
gross population density = 50,000 / 500 = 100 people/ha;
net population density = 50,000 / 250 = 200 people/ha;
per-capita land = 500 x 10000 / 50,000 = 100 m2/person (new city standard 85-105, so it passes).

map.：用地 100 ha，目标人均 100 m²/人，居住用地占比 50%（50 h:
Land of 100 ha with a target 100 m2/person and residential land at 50% (50 ha) and a target net density of 600 people/ha:
capacity by per-capita land = 100 x 10000 / 100 = 10,000 people;
capacity by net density = 50 x 600 = 30,000 people;
appropriate capacity = min(10000, 30000) = 10,000 people (limited by per-capita land, giving an actual 100 m2/person).
